 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "In this PR, `IsCoveringMap.monodromyNatTrans` (Functoriality.lean:114) carries no `@[expose]`, yet `monodromyNatTrans_app` (Functoriality.lean:128-133) is proved `(rfl)` in the same module and must unfold that body. Same pattern at `Homeomorph.compFiberEquiv` (210, no expose) with `compFiberEquiv_apply_coe := (rfl)` (219-222), `IsCoveringMap.monodromyNatIso` (169) with `monodromyNatIso_hom := (rfl)` (187-191), and `ContinuousMap.fiberMap` (56) with `fiberMap_apply_coe := (rfl)` (66-69). Grep for `fundamentalGroupEquivFiber` shows Opposite.lean:158 as the sole external use, via `rw`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Homotopy/Covering.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[expose]` and change the two proofs at lines 148 and 156 from `:= rfl` to `:= (rfl)`. No consumer needs the body: the only downstream use, `Deck/FundamentalGroup/Opposite.lean:158`, goes through `rw [IsCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquivFiber_apply_coe]` rather than unfolding.",
   "issue": "`@[expose]` on `_root_.IsCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquivFiber` publishes the `Equiv` body. The PR description defends it as unavoidable \u2014 \"Removing it breaks the two characteristic lemmas it was meant to protect \u2014 both are `rfl` and need the `Equiv` body \u2014 so the two are mutually exclusive without restructuring.\" That dichotomy is false: a non-exposed body is still visible inside its own module, and the parenthesized `(rfl)` form is what this PR uses everywhere else for exactly this shape of lemma.",
   "line": 109
  }
 ],
